  "claude": {
    "authorization": "Direct human approval of 24 logging-only files,198300 bytes, to Anthropic for read-only review",
    "initialVerdict": "CHANGES_REQUIRED",
    "initialRequiredFindings": [
      {
        "id": "T02-R1",
        "path": "implementations/csharp/src/CIS.Core/Logging/Runtime/OutputEventQueue.cs",
        "issue": "After the stop deadline, the worker can still start new flush I/O with the already-cancelled output token. AbandonUnstarted only removes registrations whose target >= firstAbandonedSequence. A registration at the in-flight sequence k stays registered. That is the final stop boundary when no queued tail exists, or an earlier periodic/FlushAsync boundary. When the uncooperative write k later completes, ProcessAsync finds First().Key <= writtenCount and calls flush!(ioCancellation.Token) with a cancelled token. The configured writers forward that token: ConsoleOutputWriter -> stream.FlushAsync(token), FileOutputWriter -> FileStream.FlushAsync(token). Real Stream, MemoryStream and FileStream implementations return an immediately cancelled task for a pre-cancelled token. The queue then faults with live LastFaultCode \"FlushFailed\" for a flush that never ran. Legacy delegates ignore the token, so they would start genuinely new post-deadline flush I/O. This is new I/O after the deadline, not cancellation of in-flight I/O. It also creates a misleading fault and is newly introduced by T02 token plumbing. The fixture misses it: HeldStream.FlushAsync never checks the token up front, and no mode combines a single in-flight configured write with a remaining reachable registration. T01's blocked case uses legacy writers.",
        "fix": "Once stop-deadline cancellation is requested, do not start a new flush. Resolve every unstarted registration as unavailable (Failed) without I/O. For example, AbandonUnstarted sets a queue-level 'deadlineExpired' flag under the gate. ProcessAsync checks that flag before selecting a flush request: it resolves the request false, removes it and continues or exits. It does not call flush. Keep the already-started 'flushing' registration unresolved until its actual I/O settles, as now. Add a stop-drain mode with one configured write held uncooperatively and no queued tail, and a stream that honors a pre-cancelled token. Assert frozen pending=1/flush Pending, then after release: flushes==0, the registration resolves Failed, no FlushFailed fault and no registered controls. Update stop-drain.md's 'Earlier reachable flush boundaries retain their existing worker coordination' sentence to match."
      },
      {
        "id": "T02-R2",
        "path": "implementations/csharp/src/CIS.Core/Logging/CoreLogRuntime.cs",
        "issue": "Public StopAsync XML documentation does not describe the new T02 public behavior. At the original deadline, accepted records that have not started are discarded (Abandoned). Cancellation of in-flight writer I/O is requested. A result can be Completion=Completed with Succeeded=false and LossObserved=true when every covered record was abandoned. The current remarks only say a timed-out observation can retain pending I/O. AGENTS.md requires documented public behavior.",
        "fix": "Extend the StopAsync <remarks>. At expiry, unstarted accepted records are abandoned and reported as Abandoned. In-flight write/flush cancellation is requested but not guaranteed. No retry or replacement writer runs. Completed means terminal dispositions, not success."
      },
      {
        "id": "T02-R3",
        "path": "planning/logging/shutdown-implementation-notes.md",
        "issue": "This file is linked from stop-drain.md as 'shutdown progress' and is now stale. 'Required following work' still says T02 must implement abandonment and that 'Existing writer delegates do not yet accept a cancellation token'. The carried review finding about resolving the original final flush registration is still listed as open. This contradicts the implemented T02 state, against the AGENTS.md rule to distinguish implemented behavior from evidence.",
        "fix": "Update the T02 paragraphs to state what is implemented, with the scoped test counts (8 unit + 7 child). State that full Developer/native qualification and review are pending, not passed. Keep the T03/T04/T05 obligations explicit, and add the new cleanup-error source (see carriedForward) to T04."
      }
    ],
